1,"Naga, Sangtam Language (NSA)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nsa,"Sangtam Naga is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Naga, Sangtam",Sino-Tibetan
